WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.301 --> 00:00:02.302 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It´s always
such a delight to see you.

00:00:02.302 --> 00:00:04.437 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
-We met in 2004...

00:00:04.437 --> 00:00:06.239 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes, we did.
-...on the set of a film

00:00:06.239 --> 00:00:08.641
that not a lot of people have
seen, called "See This Movie."

00:00:08.641 --> 00:00:10.176 align:start size:94% position:6%
Ironically called
"See This Movie."

00:00:10.176 --> 00:00:12.145 align:start size:94% position:6%
-"See This Movie."
-Where we played film --

00:00:12.145 --> 00:00:13.913 align:start size:94% position:6%
Look at the --
Look how young we are.

00:00:13.913 --> 00:00:16.116 align:start size:94% position:6%
Couple of young film students.
-Look at all the hope.

00:00:16.116 --> 00:00:17.417 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:17.417 --> 00:00:20.186 align:start size:94% position:6%
-This movie was so long ago,
pictures were blurry.

00:00:20.186 --> 00:00:21.788 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, they really were.
-Yeah, yeah.

00:00:21.788 --> 00:00:23.356 align:start size:94% position:6%
That´s before HD.

00:00:23.356 --> 00:00:24.657 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And that´s John Cho
right there.

00:00:24.657 --> 00:00:25.658 size:75% position:38%
-And John Cho, yeah.

00:00:25.658 --> 00:00:26.860 align:start size:94% position:6%
The great John Cho
in the middle.

00:00:26.860 --> 00:00:28.661 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-I also --

00:00:28.661 --> 00:00:30.196 align:start size:94% position:6%
We´re working on
a show together.

00:00:30.196 --> 00:00:31.731 align:start size:94% position:6%
You´re doing the hard work.
-Yes.

00:00:31.731 --> 00:00:34.034
-You´re a cast member
on a new show called "A.P. Bio."

00:00:34.034 --> 00:00:35.635 align:start size:94% position:6%
that´s gonna be
on NBC in February.

00:00:35.635 --> 00:00:37.804 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-And you were here --

00:00:37.804 --> 00:00:39.105 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yeah, give it up for a show
you haven´t seen.

00:00:39.105 --> 00:00:40.974 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, it´s...
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:40.974 --> 00:00:43.109 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Give it up for a show
that has yet to be scheduled.

00:00:43.109 --> 00:00:45.812
-We could´ve just made that up.
But, yeah, applaud.

00:00:45.812 --> 00:00:47.147 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That was a test.
-Yeah. Why not?

00:00:47.147 --> 00:00:50.183
-But you came out --
There´s a thing called upfronts.

00:00:50.183 --> 00:00:51.451 align:start size:94% position:6%
That´s where
we saw each other last.

00:00:51.451 --> 00:00:53.153 align:start size:94% position:6%
-The last --
And I´d never done upfronts.

00:00:53.153 --> 00:00:54.421
Upfronts is where you come

00:00:54.421 --> 00:00:57.057
and you talk to affiliates
and press about the show.

00:00:57.057 --> 00:00:59.259 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I did not know
that it was a morn--

00:00:59.259 --> 00:01:02.796 align:start size:94% position:6%
it was a dawn-till-dusk,
just nonstop gab fest

00:01:02.796 --> 00:01:04.831 size:81% position:41%
where you´re basically
selling your product.

00:01:04.831 --> 00:01:07.434 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I didn´t see you that day
till the end of the night

00:01:07.434 --> 00:01:09.636 align:start size:94% position:6%
at that restaurant
where we all got together.

00:01:09.636 --> 00:01:11.671 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so when I --
And I was so happy to see you,

00:01:11.671 --> 00:01:18.044
but I had so been stuck in my
head, in selling the show mode

00:01:18.044 --> 00:01:20.280
that our conversation --
I was so afraid afterward.

00:01:20.280 --> 00:01:22.682
Like, "He thinks I´m psychotic."

00:01:22.682 --> 00:01:23.817 align:start size:94% position:6%
Because you were --

00:01:23.817 --> 00:01:25.185 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was like,
"Hey, man, good to see you."

00:01:25.185 --> 00:01:26.586
"It´s great to see you, Seth.

00:01:26.586 --> 00:01:28.521 align:start size:94% position:6%
And this restaurant
is fantastic.

00:01:28.521 --> 00:01:31.057 align:start size:94% position:6%
The food here is so..."
[ Laughter ]

00:01:31.057 --> 00:01:32.826 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don´t even remember
what I said.

00:01:32.826 --> 00:01:36.329 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was just in that weird
non-human way of --

00:01:36.329 --> 00:01:37.597 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was like
I was trying to sell you

00:01:37.597 --> 00:01:39.532 align:start size:94% position:6%
on the wonder
of hanging out with me.

00:01:39.532 --> 00:01:41.134 align:start size:94% position:6%
Even though
we were already hanging out.

00:01:41.134 --> 00:01:43.069 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was the saddest --
-That was not my take on it.

00:01:43.069 --> 00:01:44.504 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No.
Okay, good, good.

00:01:44.504 --> 00:01:45.572 align:start size:94% position:6%
My God.

00:01:45.572 --> 00:01:47.373 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You and your co-star,
Glenn Howerton

00:01:47.373 --> 00:01:48.741 align:start size:94% position:6%
were on the red carpet.
-Yeah.

00:01:48.741 --> 00:01:50.877
-I remember us talking
about this at the dinner.

00:01:50.877 --> 00:01:53.246 size:78% position:39%
Because E! was talk--

00:01:53.246 --> 00:01:55.415
They were interviewing people
about the 10th anniversary

00:01:55.415 --> 00:01:57.350 align:start size:94% position:6%
of the Kardashians.
-Yes they were.

00:01:57.350 --> 00:02:00.753 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And you guys
have a new show on NBC.

00:02:00.753 --> 00:02:02.055 align:start size:94% position:6%
So new --
You´re new to the network.

00:02:02.055 --> 00:02:03.590 align:start size:94% position:6%
You did not realize
that E! and NBC

00:02:03.590 --> 00:02:04.791
are owned by the same company.

00:02:04.791 --> 00:02:06.059 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No idea.

00:02:06.059 --> 00:02:08.761 size:84% position:42%
And so we´re going down
the carpet and talking,

00:02:08.761 --> 00:02:11.364 size:88% position:44%
and then E! says, "Hey,
can we get your thoughts

00:02:11.364 --> 00:02:12.932
on the 10th-year anniversary

00:02:12.932 --> 00:02:14.968 align:start size:94% position:6%
of ´Keeping Up
With the Kardashians´?"

00:02:14.968 --> 00:02:16.269 align:start size:94% position:6%
And Glenn said,

00:02:16.269 --> 00:02:18.738 align:start size:94% position:6%
"I would rather cut my scrotum
off with a razor blade."

00:02:18.738 --> 00:02:20.974 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
And this is on camera.

00:02:20.974 --> 00:02:23.543 size:88% position:44%
Like they´re talking --
"Oh, well, I mean, uh...

00:02:23.543 --> 00:02:27.080
You know, it´s -- You´re both
kind of on the same network."

00:02:27.080 --> 00:02:31.017
And you could see Glenn´s face
realizing what he had just done.

00:02:31.017 --> 00:02:32.352 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then he --

00:02:32.352 --> 00:02:35.622 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, you could hear the gears
grinding of him going,

00:02:35.622 --> 00:02:37.957
"But 10 years is impressive,

00:02:37.957 --> 00:02:39.759 align:start size:94% position:6%
whether or not
I want to talk about it."

00:02:39.759 --> 00:02:42.562 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was the --
And I am beside him, like,

00:02:42.562 --> 00:02:44.230
just trying -- it was the --

00:02:44.230 --> 00:02:46.132 align:start size:94% position:6%
maybe the worst save
I´ve ever seen.

00:02:46.132 --> 00:02:47.734 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-But it was beautiful.

00:02:47.734 --> 00:02:50.336
It was one of the best --
Oh, I loved it so much.

00:02:50.336 --> 00:02:51.504 align:start size:94% position:6%
So funny.
-So congratulations

00:02:51.504 --> 00:02:54.374
on your special, "Annihilation."
-Thank you.

00:02:54.374 --> 00:02:56.376
-Obviously, we saw in the clip,
it´s a little bit about,

00:02:56.376 --> 00:02:57.877 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know,
the world we´re living in now.

00:02:57.877 --> 00:02:59.979 align:start size:94% position:6%
But you also had
an incredibly difficult year.

00:02:59.979 --> 00:03:01.381 size:81% position:41%
Your wife passed away.

00:03:01.381 --> 00:03:03.683 align:start size:94% position:6%
And you talk about that
at length.

00:03:03.683 --> 00:03:06.920 align:start size:94% position:6%
Certainly, my condolences,
our condolences.

00:03:06.920 --> 00:03:09.489 align:start size:94% position:6%
The title -- was that --
Was it hard to pick the title,

00:03:09.489 --> 00:03:11.858 align:start size:94% position:6%
or was it...?
-You know, I didn´t really --

00:03:11.858 --> 00:03:13.960 align:start size:94% position:6%
I didn´t really come up
with the title

00:03:13.960 --> 00:03:17.197 size:84% position:42%
until I was a week away
from doing the special.

00:03:17.197 --> 00:03:19.799
Because that´s how it felt to me
at that point,

00:03:19.799 --> 00:03:21.067 size:81% position:41%
in terms of the world,

00:03:21.067 --> 00:03:23.203 align:start size:94% position:6%
how if the world
had been annihilated,

00:03:23.203 --> 00:03:25.271
and then in talking about
what I´d gone through,

00:03:25.271 --> 00:03:29.075 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was taken back emotionally
to April of 2016,

00:03:29.075 --> 00:03:32.145 align:start size:94% position:6%
and that was where I felt like
I had been annihilated.

00:03:32.145 --> 00:03:33.680 align:start size:94% position:6%
There were months
where I wasn´t even sure

00:03:33.680 --> 00:03:36.015
if I was alive, basically.

00:03:36.015 --> 00:03:39.118 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then, so, as a --
almost as a joke

00:03:39.118 --> 00:03:41.921 align:start size:94% position:6%
on top of those
two very dark concepts was --

00:03:41.921 --> 00:03:45.291
You know, the comedian speak of
"Oh, I killed, I annihilated."

00:03:45.291 --> 00:03:47.260 size:81% position:41%
So I was like, "Okay.
I´ll put that in there

00:03:47.260 --> 00:03:49.262 size:84% position:42%
almost as an ironic..."

00:03:49.262 --> 00:03:51.231 align:start size:94% position:6%
Because I was so terrified of
"What if I go out

00:03:51.231 --> 00:03:54.834 align:start size:94% position:6%
and tape this special
and it just bombs horribly

00:03:54.834 --> 00:03:57.470 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I´m not able
to make this stuff funny?"

00:03:57.470 --> 00:04:00.173 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so I just --
I almost put that in there

00:04:00.173 --> 00:04:02.575 align:start size:94% position:6%
as a reverse good-luck charm,
maybe?

00:04:02.575 --> 00:04:04.244 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-If that make sense.

00:04:04.244 --> 00:04:06.145 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Obviously, you know,
for people who don´t know,

00:04:06.145 --> 00:04:08.114 align:start size:94% position:6%
when you do a special,
you´re working that material

00:04:08.114 --> 00:04:09.949 align:start size:94% position:6%
for so long, so many nights.
-Yes.

00:04:09.949 --> 00:04:11.851 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Not only obviously
you´re working towards

00:04:11.851 --> 00:04:14.087 align:start size:94% position:6%
having a product that
you´re proud to show people.

00:04:14.087 --> 00:04:16.789
Was it incredibly cathartic for
you to go through that process

00:04:16.789 --> 00:04:18.191 align:start size:94% position:6%
of talking
about this thing onstage?

00:04:18.191 --> 00:04:20.627 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, once I actually
got onstage --

00:04:20.627 --> 00:04:24.964
It was horrible, the hours
and minutes leading up to it.

00:04:24.964 --> 00:04:26.065 align:start size:94% position:6%
It got to the point
where I´m like,

00:04:26.065 --> 00:04:27.267 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Just let me go out there
and tape this,"

00:04:27.267 --> 00:04:29.202 align:start size:94% position:6%
because the tension
was killing me.

00:04:29.202 --> 00:04:32.138 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then, once I got out there
and it started going,

00:04:32.138 --> 00:04:35.074
and when you do a special,
if you´ve really worked it,

00:04:35.074 --> 00:04:37.410 size:84% position:42%
the special takes over,
and it´s almost like

00:04:37.410 --> 00:04:40.046
you ride the material itself.

00:04:40.046 --> 00:04:42.215
That sounds very hippie-esque.

00:04:42.215 --> 00:04:44.117 align:start size:94% position:6%
I´m sorry about that.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:44.117 --> 00:04:45.285
You know what you do, man?

00:04:45.285 --> 00:04:48.521 align:start size:94% position:6%
You catch a laughter wave.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:48.521 --> 00:04:51.057 align:start size:94% position:6%
And you get on your --
you get on your --

00:04:51.057 --> 00:04:52.692
get on your smile surfboard.

00:04:52.692 --> 00:04:53.860 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah.

00:04:53.860 --> 00:04:55.061
-And you know what you do?

00:04:55.061 --> 00:04:57.764
You ride it into chuckle beach.
That´s what I...

00:04:57.764 --> 00:05:00.967
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:00.967 --> 00:05:03.536
No, but, like, you know --

00:05:03.536 --> 00:05:06.005
But I didn´t know,
´cause I was so in my own head.

00:05:06.005 --> 00:05:07.974 align:start size:94% position:6%
Even doing it, I´m like,
"What if I don´t --

00:05:07.974 --> 00:05:10.109 align:start size:94% position:6%
What if the stuff
doesn´t take over?"

00:05:10.109 --> 00:05:12.312
But it did.
It´s like, "This is what I do,"

00:05:12.312 --> 00:05:13.546 size:84% position:42%
and it was this very --

00:05:13.546 --> 00:05:15.848
It was almost like
the life force asserting itself,

00:05:15.848 --> 00:05:19.319
going, "Yes, you´ve gone
through all of this hell,

00:05:19.319 --> 00:05:22.088 align:start size:94% position:6%
but you´re still a comedian,
and this is what you do."

00:05:22.088 --> 00:05:23.923 align:start size:94% position:6%
And just that felt
really amazing to me.

00:05:23.923 --> 00:05:25.625 size:84% position:42%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:25.625 --> 00:05:26.959 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It´s wonderful.

